<div class="flex-col sm:flex-row sm:gap-x-4 lg:gap-x-10 bg-transparent flex gap-y-4">
  <div class="w-full sm:w-1/2">
    <h2>The RIPE Community</h2>
    <div class="richtext">
  <p data-block-key="gvtz3">RIPE is a forum open to everyone interested in the operation of the Internet. Since 1989, it has brought together people and communities to share information and ideas, discuss best common practices, and carry out technical coordination work.</p>
</div>

    
      
<div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 mt-6">
  
    
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/community/" >About RIPE<span><i class="icon icon-tiny icon-arrow-right"></i></span></a>

    
  
    
      <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/community/wg/" >RIPE Working Groups<span><i class="icon icon-tiny icon-arrow-right"></i></span></a>

    
  
</div>

    
  </div>
  
  
<figure class="sm:w-1/2">
  
  
    
      <picture><source srcset="/media/images/RIPE-Community-.2e16d0ba.format-webp.fill-1024x576-c100.webp" type="image/webp"><img alt="The RIPE Community" class="aspect-video w-full rounded-lg" height="500" src="/media/images/RIPE-Community-P.2e16d0ba.format-jpeg.fill-1024x576-c100.jpg" width="890"></picture>
    
  
  
</figure>



</div>
</div>
        
      
        
          <div class="block-ripe_labs">

<div id="ripe-labs-d527e9ed-08a2-4278-ae6a-7a14a4a3f85b" class="bg-transparent">
  <div class="w-full sm:w-4/5 md:w-3/5 mb-6">
    <h2>RIPE Labs</h2>
    <div class="richtext">
  <p data-block-key="kfccx">Insights, ideas and analysis from across the RIPE community.</p>
</div>

    <a class="btn btn-primary mt-6" href="https://labs.ripe.net/" target='_blank'>RIPE Labs<span><i class="icon icon-tiny icon-external"></i></span></a>

  </div>
  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-10">
    
      <div class="flex flex-col shadow-lg rounded-lg bg-white card-outline">
        
          <img src="https://labs.ripe.net/media/images/iStock-92883867.2e16d0ba.fill-868x384.jpg"
               alt="Two Providers, a Stubborn Plateau and a Very Long Tail: Email in the Tranco Top-1M"
               loading="lazy"
               class="w-full object-cover rounded-t-lg" />
        
        <div class="flex flex-col flex-1 px-5">
          <a class="btn btn-textual block-item-title mb-2 font-bold text-lg" href="https://labs.ripe.net/author/artem-berezin/two-providers-a-stubborn-plateau-and-a-very-long-tail-email-in-the-tranco-top-1m/" target='_blank'>Two Providers, a Stubborn Plateau and a Very Long Tail: Email in the Tranco Top-1M<span><i class="icon icon-tiny icon-external"></i></span></a>


          <p class="text-sm text-neutral-soft leading-relaxed">
            Ten years of DNS measurements reveal three trends across the Internet&#x27;s most popular domains: email continues to consolidate around two providers, DMARC enforcement has hit a plateau, and a surprisingly large long tail of infrastructure defies easy classification.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 p-5 border-t">
          <img src="https://labs.ripe.net/media/images/IMG_7330.jpg.2e16d0ba.fill-96x96.png"
               alt="Artem Berezin"
               loading="lazy"
               class="w-10 h-10 rounded-full object-cover border-2 border-ncc-medium" />
          <div class="flex flex-col min-w-0">
            <a class="btn btn-textual text-sm font-semibold py-0" href="https://labs.ripe.net/author/artem-berezin/" target='_blank'>Artem Berezin<span><i class="icon icon-tiny icon-external"></i></span></a>


            
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    
      <div class="flex flex-col shadow-lg rounded-lg bg-white card-outline">
        
          <img src="https://labs.ripe.net/media/images/Gemini_Generated_Image_6op8xc6op8x.2e16d0ba.fill-868x384.jpg"
               alt="What&#x27;s ARP Got to Do with It?"
               loading="lazy"
               class="w-full object-cover rounded-t-lg" />
        
        <div class="flex flex-col flex-1 px-5">
          <a class="btn btn-textual block-item-title mb-2 font-bold text-lg" href="https://labs.ripe.net/author/remco-van-mook/whats-arp-got-to-do-with-it/" target='_blank'>What&#x27;s ARP Got to Do with It?<span><i class="icon icon-tiny icon-external"></i></span></a>


          <p class="text-sm text-neutral-soft leading-relaxed">
            It&#x27;s only ARP. It works. So how much can it really matter? The answer lies beyond ARP itself, in the IPv4 layer cake that grew around it over four decades. The IPv4 internet is not going away in bounded time, and nobody should pretend otherwise.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 p-5 border-t">
          <img src="https://labs.ripe.net/media/images/remco.2e16d0ba.fill-96x96.jpg"
               alt="Remco van Mook"
               loading="lazy"
               class="w-10 h-10 rounded-full object-cover border-2 border-ncc-medium" />
          <div class="flex flex-col min-w-0">
            <a class="btn btn-textual text-sm font-semibold py-0" href="https://labs.ripe.net/author/remco-van-mook/" target='_blank'>Remco van Mook<span><i class="icon icon-tiny icon-external"></i></span></a>


            
              <span class="text-xs text-neutral-soft">community contributor</span>
            
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    
      <div class="flex flex-col shadow-lg rounded-lg bg-white card-outline">
        
          <img src="https://labs.ripe.net/media/images/iStock-2086178405.2e16d0ba.fill-868x384.jpg"
               alt="Inside a Shutdown: BGP Evidence from an Operator Who Was There"
               loading="lazy"
               class="w-full object-cover rounded-t-lg" />
        
        <div class="flex flex-col flex-1 px-5">
          <a class="btn btn-textual block-item-title mb-2 font-bold text-lg" href="https://labs.ripe.net/author/mdkamruzzaman-khan-2/inside-a-shutdown-bgp-evidence-from-an-operator-who-was-there/" target='_blank'>Inside a Shutdown: BGP Evidence from an Operator Who Was There<span><i class="icon icon-tiny icon-external"></i></span></a>


          <p class="text-sm text-neutral-soft leading-relaxed">
            When Bangladesh vanished from the global routing table in July 2024, public routing data captured the event as it unfolded. Drawing on first-hand observations from inside one affected network, this article explores what that data can and cannot tell us.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 p-5 border-t">
          <img src="None"
               alt="Md.Kamruzzaman Khan"
               loading="lazy"
               class="w-10 h-10 rounded-full object-cover border-2 border-ncc-medium" />
          <div class="flex flex-col min-w-0">
            <a class="btn btn-textual text-sm font-semibold py-0" href="https://labs.ripe.net/author/mdkamruzzaman-khan-2/" target='_blank'>Md.Kamruzzaman Khan<span><i class="icon icon-tiny icon-external"></i></span></a>


            
              <span class="text-xs text-neutral-soft">community contributor</span>
            
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    

    
  </div>
</div>
</div>
        
      
        
